  recipeId: memory
  concept: 'Authored objective: Sign the final cold-start audit.

    Authored requirement:
    After an isolated restart collect fresh power, POST, device and thermal evidence
    on the same boot.

    General teaching principle: Memory and initialization
    workflows require checking power, connectivity, configuration and the authored
    test responses in the correct sequence.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A staged startup checklist helps distinguish a missing prerequisite from
    a later failure.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: One passing startup indicator does not guarantee every memory or
    firmware check has passed.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Sign the final cold-start audit\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Sign the final cold-start audit\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 130, perform the objective \u2018Sign the final cold-start
    audit\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: After
    an isolated restart collect fresh power, POST, device and thermal evidence on
    the same boot.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does
    not grade your answer."
